WEBVTT

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:08.610
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.940
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.650
but also in crime.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.910
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.330
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.500
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:49.190
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.940
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:01.290
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:07.630
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:12.170
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:19.680
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.810
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.640
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.860
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:36.110
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:42.330
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:47.750
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.090
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.430
The black giant has landed.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:07.310
Alphonse was given a riot gun
to use against the Griffin...

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.770
but Noa couldn't fire it
because of civilian bystanders.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:14.320
Then Three-S tried to eliminate
the evidence against Shaft...

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.360
by placing explosives
on the Griffin's back.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.530
But the charges were
set off prematurely.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.370
The shock of the blast caused
Noa to black out briefly...

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.250
but Asuma and the
team woke her in time.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.670
And now, the Griffin
is advancing again!

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.970
Griffin Down!

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.260
You lose!

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.600
The only loser here -

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.100
IS YOU!

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.150
Counterattack!
Go, Noa!

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.360
Step out of your machine!

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:03.910
It can't be!

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:14.040
Chief!
I'm glad you're safe.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:19.050
This is all thanks to Three-S.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:21.800
What's wrong?

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.510
That sound coming
from the Griffin...

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.680
It isn't supposed
to sound like that.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.850
I'll find out what's happening.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.400
Yes, I hear it, too.
It definitely isn't normal.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:42.780
Anyway, what's going on?
I thought I heard an explosion.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.120
I won't be held
responsible for this!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:52.210
The explosion damaged it.
It was that damned Three-S!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.840
Let go!

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.460
I'll never let go.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:06.760
A little higher.
Good, don't move!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:10.430
Careful, Yamazaki, the
cylinder's going to rotate.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.890
Yes, right!

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.600
Come on -

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:26.120
Damn!
He got my main monitor!

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:36.920
Yamazaki!

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.880
Even in your Ingram
you wouldn't have hit him.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.510
Shut up!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.220
Are you okay?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.390
I'll be fine, but we won't
be able to fire another shot.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.140
My monitor's out.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:59.270
Don't let go, Noa! You're blind.
You'll never catch him again!

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.070
My ribs!

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.030
That's why I told you to
stay home and rest.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:05.490
I couldn't do that!

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:09.450
You must have heard that.
Can you keep going?

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.200
I want to run away.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:12.870
But you know you can't.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.290
Noa, to your right!

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.170
Here?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.460
Why you!

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.090
Why you!

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.820
I don't believe it.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.070
It's like two children fighting.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:51.740
Mr. Sakaki, how much power
is left in the Ingram?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.870
No more than a few minutes.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:59.000
Noa, shut down all
unnecessary systems.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.930
Main monitor off;
sensor 3, no good.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:15.850
This can't be happening!

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.310
Right manipulator gone.
Shutting it down.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.780
My Griffin's being destroyed!
It's not fair!

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.530
Power train - still good.
One more run should stop him.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.990
You can do it, Alphonse!

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.540
Machine 1 first,
move in to reinforce.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.500
Bud, time to go.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.250
Chief!

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:53.260
Bud, that's enough.
Time to escape.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:53.970
What?

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.890
Luck wasn't with us.
The Griffin isn't looking too good.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.940
It's no longer a fair fight.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:06.400
No, no!

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:15.450
The fight has sunk to a new low!

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.290
The Labors are now
engaged in a slugfest!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:21.120
This is terrible!
It's unbelievable!

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:23.210
Ridiculous!

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:33.680
Why you!

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.220
Why you!

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.890
Out of my way!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:49.860
Bud Renard Harchand, be a
good boy. It's time to go.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.450
Do you want the
police to catch you?

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.530
We have to abandon Bud.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:00.950
The Griffin's been trashed,
and if we don't escape soon...

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:03.250
the police will close in on us.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:08.090
We have to abandon Bud and
the Griffin, and get you to safety.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:09.460
Kurosaki!

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:14.260
If you survive, Planning
Division 7 will live again.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.320
I'll never let go.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.330
I think Bud's
finally ready to go.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:40.910
We should be leaving, too.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:45.620
What happened?

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.000
He detached his arm!

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.050
That machine has
all sorts of tricks.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:55.720
That seems to be its trademark.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.590
The hatch won't open!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.680
Noa, 11 o'clock!

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:04.850
You won't get away!

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.740
This doesn't mean that I lost!

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.710
He doesn't have enough speed!
He's going to crash into the bay.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:34.880
Who are you calling?

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:38.300
I'm going to ask the
Far East Manager to pick up Bud.

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.560
I can't gain altitude!
I'm going to crash!

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:14.760
That's a bad sign. Motor tension
is dropping as the battery fades.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:24.970
Noa!

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.410
What's the matter?

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.120
Are you hurt?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.580
He got...

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.830
He got away.
After all I did.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:08.640
This Ingram is one solid machine.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.480
The economy model I used
in Haruumi just fell apart.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:17.980
I really wanted to run away...

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.030
but I stayed and fought.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:29.000
Remember how brave you were today
and you'll always put up a good fight.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.960
I don't want a good fight.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:39.550
I guess you're right.
There's no such thing as a good fight.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:47.560
How's Izumi?

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.350
Give her a few minutes.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.940
That girl infuriates me.
She had that great gun -

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:57.230
I know how you feel, but you
didn't do the fighting. She did.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:58.360
But...

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:02.860
Ota, Yamazaki, thanks to you,
Izumi wasn't crushed.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:03.610
Good work.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.450
Captain, I would have...

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:09.200
Everyone has his own style.
That's how it is...

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:17.670
Sorry about this.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.760
It'll cost plenty
in overtime pay.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:23.380
We'll have to send this one
back to the factory, too.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:26.090
Carefully, please!
Carefully!

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.640
You know something?

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.560
I think you've changed.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:37.520
Have I?

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:41.110
To be honest, I never
thought you'd get this far.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.360
Neither did I.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.260
There he is!

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:17.730
Positive ID: Bud Renard Harchand.
Prepare to retrieve.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:30.870
Hello?

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:37.790
Utsumi here! I hope you weren't
stuck in that office all night long!

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:41.170
Damn you! This is all
your doing! But what now?

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:42.800
What <i>should</i> I do?

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.840
Where's the Griffin?

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.220
Answer me, Utsumi!

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:52.560
Calm down.
Bud Renard escaped...

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.390
and the Griffin's now at
the bottom of Tokyo Bay.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:14:00.110
By the way, I'll be
coming in to the office today.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.650
I'll arrange for Three-S to
handle a few minor details.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:26.010
Colonel, I've left
a few observers.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.170
All other teams have
completed withdrawal.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:32.430
I've just heard
from the Chairman.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.310
The Chairman?

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.350
Utsumi is still a valuable asset.
We are to leave him alone.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:39.350
Then what was the
point of this debacle?

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.610
We have our orders.
"Theirs not to reason why..."

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.980
Planning Division 7 must
be pretty damned important.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.870
Miss Izumi, we're here.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:05.630
Miss Izumi?

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:10.050
Where's Asuma?

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:16.510
He forgot his medicine, so he's
stopping off at the dorm to pick it up.

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:21.440
Mr. Sakaki offered to
swing him by in his car.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:29.360
It wouldn't be so bad,
if you'd behaved yourself.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.610
Ouch!

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:35.120
I hope he'll be all right.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.160
He's young.
He'll recover.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.290
Today we're going
to start a test drive.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:43.170
Let's check the power train first.
Start charging the battery.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.250
Charging battery.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:47.670
Thanks to Alphonse,
I didn't get a scratch.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.380
The Ingram is an
amazing machine.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.220
Shige, you can fix
him, can't you?

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:56.550
Compared to Ota's machine,
this one's barely scratched.

00:15:56.550 --> 00:16:00.730
The backbone's still okay, and
it could move if we had power.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.690
It'll be as good as
new in no time.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:05.150
Thank you so much.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.480
Leave it to us.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:15.620
Something should have been
done about Three-S and Shaft!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:20.330
Ota, if you have something
to say, spit it out!

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.620
How can we leave
before the job's done?

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:28.290
We let our opponents
just walk away!

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:31.880
We've lost every single Labor.
What could we do?

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:35.800
But Kanuka stayed behind,
and she's still working!

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:42.810
Kanuka's job is different.
She's investigating for the NYPD.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.480
So what exactly IS our job?

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.190
The mobile police
handles the crisis.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:52.320
The detectives handle the cleanup.
It's time to rest.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:54.150
You hear me, Ota?

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.910
In only three days,
Division 2 has been wiped out.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:01.370
I'm getting a headache
just about how to rebuild.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.790
Then what can I do?

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.710
You can go back to the dorm
and sleep. I'm tired, too.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:16.180
Miss Izumi, I can drop you off
at the dorm. It's on my way.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:20.010
Thanks, but I don't want
to leave my bike behind.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:23.680
I'll just take a nap
in the duty room.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.020
Take care.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.480
You too.
Hurry home.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:30.480
I'm sure your wife will
be relieved to see you.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.440
Oh, she's probably
asleep by now.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:39.030
Hello, Michiko? Oh, were you
still asleep? I'm sorry.

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:42.830
No, it's nothing, really, but did
you see the news yesterday?

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.250
Special Vehicles fought
the Black Labor!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:49.790
They even had a shot of my
husband Miki, right there on TV!

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:56.170
You missed it? He was amazing!
I could copy it for you!

00:17:56.170 --> 00:18:00.680
<i>The fight has sunk</i>
<i>to a new low!</i>

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.940
No, it's no problem!
Bye!

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:14.360
Let's see... I'd better call Mama next!
Oh, there's so much to do!

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:05.490
Geez, why do I
have to wear this?

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.620
But it looks good on you!

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:09.620
That was a low blow!

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:14.790
We're still in danger. Grin and
bear it until we're out of Japan.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:27.770
Good, I made it in time.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:32.980
Shinohara and Izumi
wanted to come...

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:36.980
but the Ingram repairs
are nearly finished.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:40.450
Are you sure you can
afford the time, Captain?

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.320
Didn't they locate a section
of the Black Labor?

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.620
You're remarkably well informed.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:51.040
Mr. Sakaki is checking into it.
It's rather strange.

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:52.290
Strange?

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:02.590
Every Labor has dozens of telltale
clues to its manufacturer.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:08.720
For example, the Ingram differs
from all other Shinohara Labors...

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:12.560
But the auto-balance unit
tags it as a Shinohara make.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.690
Exactly. But the Black Labor
lacks any such features.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:20.940
So it wasn't just an
existing model in disguise.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:23.530
Exactly.

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.910
And how did your
investigation go?

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:34.250
Three-S is now claiming to be
the victim, since they lost Labors.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.840
I tell you, if this had
happened in America...

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:41.340
Then I would have
been a lot happier!

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:48.550
I'm sure we'll meet again.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.140
Take care.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:08.870
Keep quiet!

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:17.170
Excuse me...

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:27.260
Could I trouble you for a light?

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:29.720
Light? You are meaning "fire?"

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:31.930
Yes, please.

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:35.690
Please to take candy, instead.

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:36.600
Candy?

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:39.020
Candy is better for
health than tobacco.

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:41.900
Odd. I thought I
smelled smoke on you.

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:43.150
Tobacco?

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:45.490
I smelled fire.

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:54.120
Regrettably, little can be
done about such smells.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.660
Regrettably.

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:23.400
I'm going to take
him for a test drive!

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:30.160
But first...

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:33.790
Now that you're repaired,
it's time for a little polishing!

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:35.410
She hasn't changed a bit.

00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:06.440
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:08.530 --> 00:23:14.200
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:16.160
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:21.620
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:29.920
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:32.180
I got it

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:39.730
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:45.610
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:47.150
One more chance

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:54.780
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:00.250
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:03.920
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:09.420 --> 00:24:13.430
This story is fiction...

00:24:09.420 --> 00:24:13.430
but in 10 years, who knows?

